From c2a4564d0291e15a0227ac3e7035fc7898066d93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local-agent <local@agent>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:36:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/38] kebab: boot to BDS (UFS init no longer fatal)

Three changes get the OnePlus 8T (kebab) UEFI from an ABL load error
all the way to BDS with a working graphical boot-device menu:

  * MemoryMapLib: add the missing 'CPU Vectors' region (0x9FF8C000),
    present in the shipped uefiplat.cfg but absent from the map. The
    vendor stack prints 'CPU Vectors region not present in config file'
    without it.

  * MemoryMapLib: add the missing 'UFS UFS REGS' MMIO region
    (0x01D80000, 128 KiB). Addresses verified against the device DTB
    (ufshc@1d84000, ufsphy_mem@1d87000, ufsice@1d90000 all fall inside).

  * ConfigurationMapLib: EnableUfsIOC 0 -> 1, matching the SM8250
    sibling port (alioth), which also deviates from its own uefiplat.cfg
    on this key. Without it UFSDxe asserts with 'Device Error' and
    CpuDeadLoop()s the machine.

Result: UEFI reaches BDS, draws the UI, and presents the boot device
menu. UFSDxe still reports UFS errors and no block device appears, so
booting an OS is still blocked - but the machine no longer dies.

Note: the boot image must be packed with the stock dtb pulled from the
LOS boot.img, NOT Resources/DTBs/kebab.dtb - ABL rejects the latter.
